      "slug": "redox_magnesium",
      "title": "Redox magnesium",
      "problem": "Magnesium reacts with hydrochloric acid to give magnesium\nchloride and hydrogen gas.  Write the balanced equation, the\noxidation and reduction half-equations, and find the moles of\nH2 produced when 4.8 g of Mg reacts with excess HCl.\nDraw a particle diagram of the beaker before and after.\nM(Mg) = 24.0 g/mol",
      "answer": "n(H2) = 0.20 mol",
      "dir": "chemistry/advanced/redox_magnesium",
      "images": {
        "ques": "chemistry/advanced/redox_magnesium/ques.png",
        "good": [
          "chemistry/advanced/redox_magnesium/good_1.png"
        ],
        "bad": [
          "chemistry/advanced/redox_magnesium/bad_1.png",
          "chemistry/advanced/redox_magnesium/bad_2.png",
          "chemistry/advanced/redox_magnesium/bad_3.png",
          "chemistry/advanced/redox_magnesium/bad_4.png",
          "chemistry/advanced/redox_magnesium/bad_5.png"
        ]
      },
      "solutions": [
        {
          "name": "good_1",
          "work": [
            "Unbalanced:  Mg + HCl -> MgCl2 + H2",
            "Mg + 2HCl -> MgCl2 + H2     (balanced)",
            "Oxidation:  Mg -> Mg2+ + 2e-",
            "Reduction:  2H+ + 2e- -> H2",
            "n(Mg) = 4.8 / 24.0 = 0.20 mol",
            "Mg : H2 is 1 : 1",
            "n(H2) = 0.20 mol"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "bad_1",
          "work": [
            "Mg + 2HCl -> MgCl2 + H2",
            "Oxidation:  Mg -> Mg2+ + e-",
            "Reduction:  2H+ + 2e- -> H2",
            "n(Mg) = 4.8 / 24.0 = 0.20 mol",
            "n(H2) = 0.20 mol"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "bad_2",
          "work": [
            "Mg + 2HCl -> MgCl2 + H2",
            "Oxidation:  Mg -> Mg2+ + 2e-",
            "Reduction:  2H+ + 2e- -> H2",
            "n(Mg) = 4.8 / 24.0 = 0.20 mol",
            "The equation has 2 in front, so Mg : H2 is 1 : 2",
            "n(H2) = 2 x 0.20 = 0.40 mol"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "bad_3",
          "work": [
            "Mg + 2HCl -> MgCl2 + H2",
            "Oxidation:  Mg -> Mg2+ + 2e-",
            "Reduction:  2H+ + 2e- -> H2",
            "n(Mg) = 4.8 x 24.0 = 115.2 mol",
            "n(H2) = 115.2 mol"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
